  "name": "FAIR4ML",
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/zbmed-semtec/projects/2023_FAIR4ML",
  "alternateName": "FAIR for Machine Learning",
  "description": "Machine and deep learning models have become essential research artifacts, yet machine-readable metadata describing them is often missing or buried in text-based documents. The Research Data Alliance (RDA) FAIR for Machine Learning Interest Group (FAIR4ML-IG) created FAIR4ML, an extension of the schema.org vocabulary designed to describe ML model metadata in a structured, interoperable way. The vocabulary builds on community use cases, competency questions, and analyses of metadata from platforms such as Hugging Face and OpenML. FAIR4ML is compatible with related initiatives including Bioschemas, CodeMeta, Croissant ML, and machine-actionable Software Management Plans. It is adopted by services such as MLentory (NFDI4DataScience) and InesData, and continues to be refined through hackathons and crosswalks to other schemas. At ZB MED, the Semantic Technologies team contributes to vocabulary development, metadata harmonisation, tutorials, and outreach—including the KI2025 tutorial on FAIR4ML and ML model cards.",
